     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">\r\nHi Chunyang,\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Thanks for your interest in Canopy and truly sorry for my late reply. We’ve encountered a potential issue in transforming the B allele frequency and the log-r ratio values from Sequenza to WM and Wm matrices, due to the ploidy issue. However,\r\n as stated in our manual, “<span style=\"color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:16px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">The\r\n B-allele frequency is Bf = Wm / (WM + Wm) and the depth ratio is depth.ratio = (WM + Wm)/2. From here the input matrix WM and Wm can be calculated.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:16px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"> </span>“.\r\n Maybe you can try Falcon or Falcon-X? This is by default the caller in our pipeline MARATHON <a href=\"https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792498397774000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3DR0mT0c1BI2UKebPgSSMJ\">https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON</a>.</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Hope this can be helpful to you.</div>\r\n<div>Yuchao</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n<blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n<div>On Nov 9, 2018, at 3:26 PM, Bao, Chunyang &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">Chunya...@DFCI.HARVARD.EDU</a>&gt; wrote:</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\">\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\nHi Yuchao,<u></u><u></u></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<u></u> <u></u></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\nThanks for your excellent work on<span> </span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);background-color:white;background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\">Canopy</span>! \r\n I am sort of interested in it and wondering if you could give me some advice.<u></u><u></u></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<u></u> <u></u></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\nSay that I have an Allelic CNV SEG file from GATK4/ABSOLUTE, like the output of Sequenza.  After reviewing the following documents, I am still not 100% sure how to generate W<sup>M</sup><span> </span>and W<sup>m</sup><span> </span>matrices\r\n from my allelic SEG file.  Do you have any tools to do that automatically for Sequenza? Or, are you still working on it? Any suggestions are welcome.<u></u><u></u></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<u></u> <u></u></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\nDocuments I have read (Did I missed something …?):<u></u><u></u></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<a href=\"https://github.com/yuchaojiang/Canopy/blob/master/instruction/SNA_CNA_input.md\" style=\"color:rgb(149,79,114);text-decoration:underline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/yuchaojiang/Canopy/blob/master/instruction/SNA_CNA_input.md&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792498397774000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3xEnI1Z1wb0BQTQGJ94M2f\">https://github.com/yuchaojiang/Canopy/blob/master/instruction/SNA_CNA_input.md</a><u></u><u></u></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<a href=\"https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON/blob/master/script/CODEX2_FALCONX.R\" style=\"color:rgb(149,79,114);text-decoration:underline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON/blob/master/script/CODEX2_FALCONX.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792498397774000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0PjFdGPE-D7RpoexYUE7yr\">https://github.com/yuchaojiang/MARATHON/blob/master/script/CODEX2_FALCONX.R</a><u></u><u></u></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<a href=\"https://github.com/yuchaojiang/Canopy/blob/master/instruction/falcon_demo.R\" style=\"color:rgb(149,79,114);text-decoration:underline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/yuchaojiang/Canopy/blob/master/instruction/falcon_demo.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792498397774000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2LOChjPrvmRwqC4p6Ag4Nj\">https://github.com/yuchaojiang/Canopy/blob/master/instruction/falcon_demo.R</a><u></u><u></u></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!forum/canopy_phylogeny\" style=\"color:rgb(149,79,114);text-decoration:underline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!forum/canopy_phylogeny&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792498397774000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ExJVpNVsWibx35UWMWTX0\">https://groups.google.com/forum/#!forum/canopy_phylogeny</a><u></u><u></u></div>\r\n<div style=